IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`

-- wra2-s44-jsa-commitment.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK) s 44 (and s 45), claimant commitment for jobseeker's allowance in the interim period.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part wra2. Host Act short names: JSA = Jobseekers Act 1995.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt (a converter script's plain-text rendering; not the official text).
-- A line `-- src:N | text` copies line N of that file; the `@ref` under a run of them cites the same lines.
-- Section 44 amends the Jobseekers Act 1995 for the interim period (before universal credit): it makes accepting a
-- "claimant commitment" a condition of entitlement (JSA 1(2)(b)), substitutes JSA 9 and 10, and defines "employment officer".
-- Every answer is a MAYBE BOOLEAN or a BOOLEAN: JUST FALSE / FALSE only where the text says no in its own words;
-- NOTHING where the text points outside the sources (regulations, orders, the opinion of an officer), is silent, or limits
-- a grant by its own wording and the case falls outside the limit.

§ `s 44 Claimant commitment for jobseeker's allowance`

§§ `s 44(2) JSA 1(2)(b): accepting a claimant commitment is a condition`

-- src:523 | (2) In section 1 (the jobseeker's allowance), in subsection (2)(b) for “entered into a jobseeker's agreement which remains in force” there is substituted “ accepted a claimant commitment ”.
-- src:552 | (9) Regulations may provide that, in prescribed circumstances, a claimant is to be treated as having satisfied the condition mentioned in section 1(2)(b).
@ref s 44(2) JSA 1(2)(b) with JSA 9(9) (src:523 src:552)
GIVEN `the claimant has accepted a claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations treat the claimant as having satisfied the condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(2) JSA 1(2)(b) the claimant satisfies the condition of having accepted a claimant commitment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant has accepted a claimant commitment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `regulations treat the claimant as having satisfied the condition`
            -- JSA 9(9): regulations may treat a claimant as having satisfied the condition in prescribed circumstances
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has accepted a claimant commitment" is a condition of entitlement; not accepted, and not treated as satisfied
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed circumstances are in regulations that are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 44 JSA 9: the claimant commitment`

-- src:526 | (1) For the purposes of this Act a “claimant commitment” is a record of a claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of a jobseeker's allowance.
@ref s 44 JSA 9(1) (src:526)
GIVEN `the award` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 9(1) the award is an award of a jobseeker's allowance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the award`
    WHEN `contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `income-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to an award of a jobseeker's allowance" -- an award of any other benefit is not one
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:526 | (1) For the purposes of this Act a “claimant commitment” is a record of a claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of a jobseeker's allowance.
@ref s 44 JSA 9(1) (src:526)
GIVEN `the document is a record of a claimant's responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the award the record is in relation to` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 9(1) the document is a claimant commitment` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “claimant commitment” is a record of a claimant's responsibilities in relation to an award of a jobseeker's allowance" (a definition; read as closed, see NOTES: the word is "is", not "means")
        `the document is a record of a claimant's responsibilities`
    AND `s 44 JSA 9(1) the award is an award of a jobseeker's allowance` `the award the record is in relation to`

-- src:527 | (2) A claimant commitment shall—
-- src:528 | (a) be prepared by an employment officer,
-- src:529 | (b) be in such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit,
-- src:530 | (c) include any prescribed information, and
-- src:531 | (d) include any other information an employment officer or the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include.
@ref s 44 JSA 9(2) (src:527-531)
GIVEN `who prepared the claimant commitment` IS AN Authority
      `its form is one the Secretary of State thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it includes the prescribed information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it includes the other information an employment officer or the Secretary of State considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 9(2) the claimant commitment is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall (a) be prepared by an employment officer" (a flat requirement not met)
        IF NOT (`who prepared the claimant commitment` EQUALS `an employment officer`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall (b) be in such form as the Secretary of State thinks fit"
        IF NOT `its form is one the Secretary of State thinks fit`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall (d) include any other information an employment officer or the Secretary of State considers it appropriate to include"
        IF NOT `it includes the other information an employment officer or the Secretary of State considers appropriate`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `it includes the prescribed information`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall (c) include any prescribed information"
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what information is prescribed is left to regulations
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `s 44 JSA 9(3) kind of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 44 JSA 9(3)(a) information on the conditions of availability and actively seeking employment`
    `s 44 JSA 9(3)(b) details of a requirement under regulations under section 8 or 17A or a jobseeker's direction`
    `s 44 JSA 9(3)(c) details of the consequences of a failure to comply with such a requirement`
    `s 44 JSA 9(3) some other kind of information`

-- src:532 | (3) Information included in a claimant commitment under subsection (2)(d) may include—
-- src:533 | (a) information in respect of the conditions mentioned in section 1(2)(a) and (c);
-- src:534 | (b) details of any requirement imposed on the claimant by virtue of regulations under section 8 or 17A, or under a jobseeker's direction;
-- src:535 | (c) details of any consequences of a failure to comply with such a requirement.
@ref s 44 JSA 9(3) (src:532-535)
GIVEN `the kind of information` IS A `s 44 JSA 9(3) kind of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 9(3) the information may be included under subsection (2)(d)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of information`
    WHEN `s 44 JSA 9(3)(a) information on the conditions of availability and actively seeking employment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 44 JSA 9(3)(b) details of a requirement under regulations under section 8 or 17A or a jobseeker's direction` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 44 JSA 9(3)(c) details of the consequences of a failure to comply with such a requirement` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may include" names three kinds and does not close the list
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:536 | (4) A claimant shall not be invited to accept a claimant commitment by an employment officer unless, in the opinion of the employment officer, the conditions mentioned in section 1(2)(a) and (c) would be satisfied with respect to the claimant if he were to act in accordance with, or be treated as acting in accordance with, the proposed claimant commitment.
@ref s 44 JSA 9(4) (src:536)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the employment officer the conditions in section 1(2)(a) and (c) would be satisfied if the claimant acted in accordance with the proposed claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 9(4) the claimant is not barred from being invited by an employment officer to accept the claimant commitment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `in the opinion of the employment officer the conditions in section 1(2)(a) and (c) would be satisfied if the claimant acted in accordance with the proposed claimant commitment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A claimant shall not be invited to accept a claimant commitment by an employment officer unless, in the opinion of the employment officer, the conditions ... would be satisfied"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:537 | (5) The employment officer may, and if asked to do so by the claimant shall forthwith, refer a proposed claimant commitment to the Secretary of State for him to determine—
-- src:538 | (a) whether, if the claimant were to act in accordance with the proposed claimant commitment, he would satisfy—
-- src:539 | (i) the condition mentioned in section 1(2)(a), or
-- src:540 | (ii) the condition mentioned in section 1(2)(c), and
-- src:541 | (b) whether it is reasonable to expect the claimant to have to act in accordance with the proposed claimant commitment.
@ref s 44 JSA 9(5) (src:537-541)
GIVEN `the claimant has asked the employment officer to refer the proposed claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 9(5) the employment officer must refer the proposed claimant commitment to the Secretary of State forthwith` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant has asked the employment officer to refer the proposed claimant commitment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The employment officer may, and if asked to do so by the claimant shall forthwith, refer" -- without a request the officer has a power, not a stated duty
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:542 | (6) A reference under subsection (5) may only relate to information included in the proposed claimant commitment under subsection (3)(a).
@ref s 44 JSA 9(6) (src:542)
GIVEN `the kind of information the reference relates to` IS A `s 44 JSA 9(3) kind of information`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 9(6) the reference under subsection (5) may relate to that information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of information the reference relates to`
    WHEN `s 44 JSA 9(3)(a) information on the conditions of availability and actively seeking employment` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reference under subsection (5) may only relate to information included in the proposed claimant commitment under subsection (3)(a)"
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:544 | (a) shall, so far as practicable, dispose of it in accordance with this section before the end of the period of 14 days from the date of the reference;
@ref s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) (src:544)
GIVEN `the date of the reference` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) the last day of the period of 14 days from the date of the reference` MEANS
    -- fork F-44-1 (NOTES): "from the date of the reference" excludes that day, so the 14 days run from the next day
    `the date of the reference` PLUS 14

-- src:544 | (a) shall, so far as practicable, dispose of it in accordance with this section before the end of the period of 14 days from the date of the reference;
@ref s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) (src:544)
GIVEN `the date of the reference` IS A DATE
      `the date the Secretary of State disposed of the reference` IS A DATE
      `it was practicable to dispose of it in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) the Secretary of State has disposed of the reference in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the Secretary of State disposed of the reference` AT MOST `s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) the last day of the period of 14 days from the date of the reference` `the date of the reference`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, so far as practicable, dispose of it ... before the end of the period of 14 days" -- late when it was practicable to be in time
        IF `it was practicable to dispose of it in time`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so far as practicable" -- late but not practicable to be in time
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) dispose of the reference`

-- src:544 | (a) shall, so far as practicable, dispose of it in accordance with this section before the end of the period of 14 days from the date of the reference;
@ref s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) (src:544)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) action`
`s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) the Secretary of State must dispose of the reference within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary of State`
    MUST `s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) dispose of the reference`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary of State` BECAUSE "the reference was not disposed of within 14 days from its date"

-- src:543 | (7) On a reference under subsection (5) the Secretary of State—
-- src:545 | (b) may give such directions, with respect to the terms of the proposed claimant commitment, as the Secretary of State considers appropriate;
@ref s 44 JSA 9(7)(b) (src:543 src:545)
GIVEN `a reference has been made under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 9(7)(b) the Secretary of State may give directions on the terms of the proposed claimant commitment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a reference has been made under subsection (5)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On a reference under subsection (5)" -- no reference has been made
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:546 | (c) may direct that, if such conditions as he considers appropriate are satisfied, the proposed claimant commitment is to be treated (if accepted) as having been accepted by the claimant on such date as may be specified in the direction.
@ref s 44 JSA 9(7)(c) (src:546)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has directed that the proposed claimant commitment is to be treated as accepted on a date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions the direction sets are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant accepted it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified in the direction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 44 JSA 9(7)(c) the date on which the proposed claimant commitment is treated as accepted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the Secretary of State has directed that the proposed claimant commitment is to be treated as accepted on a date`
           AND `the conditions the direction sets are satisfied`
           AND `the claimant accepted it`
        THEN JUST `the date specified in the direction`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if such conditions as he considers appropriate are satisfied ... (if accepted)" -- no direction, conditions unmet or not accepted
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:553 | (10) For the purposes of this Act a claimant accepts a claimant commitment if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it in such manner as may be prescribed.
@ref s 44 JSA 9(10) (src:553)
GIVEN `the claimant accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant accepted it in the manner prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 9(10) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "accepts a claimant commitment if, and only if, the claimant accepts the most up-to-date version of it"
        IF NOT `the claimant accepted the most up-to-date version of the claimant commitment`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the claimant accepted it in the manner prescribed`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, and only if, ... accepts ... in such manner as may be prescribed" -- accepted, but not in the prescribed manner
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the manner of acceptance is prescribed in regulations that are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 44 JSA 10: variation of the claimant commitment`

-- src:556 | (1) A claimant commitment may be varied by an employment officer.
@ref s 44 JSA 10(1) (src:556)
GIVEN `the person who varies the claimant commitment` IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 10(1) the claimant commitment may be varied by that person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person who varies the claimant commitment` EQUALS `an employment officer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be varied by an employment officer" says nothing of any other person
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:557 | (2) An employment officer shall not vary a claimant commitment unless, in the opinion of the employment officer, the conditions mentioned in section 1(2)(a) and (c) would continue to be satisfied with respect to the claimant if he were to act in accordance with, or be treated as acting in accordance with, the varied claimant commitment.
@ref s 44 JSA 10(2) (src:557)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the employment officer the conditions in section 1(2)(a) and (c) would continue to be satisfied under the varied claimant commitment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 10(2) the employment officer is not barred from varying the claimant commitment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `in the opinion of the employment officer the conditions in section 1(2)(a) and (c) would continue to be satisfied under the varied claimant commitment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An employment officer shall not vary a claimant commitment unless, in the opinion of the employment officer, the conditions ... would continue to be satisfied"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:559 | (4) For the purposes of this section a “relevant variation” of a claimant commitment means a variation which relates to information to be included in the claimant commitment in respect of the conditions mentioned in section 1(2)(a) and (c).
@ref s 44 JSA 10(4) (src:559)
GIVEN `the variation relates to information to be included in respect of the conditions in section 1(2)(a) and (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 10(4) the variation is a relevant variation` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “relevant variation” of a claimant commitment means a variation which relates to information to be included in the claimant commitment in respect of the conditions mentioned in section 1(2)(a) and (c)"
    `the variation relates to information to be included in respect of the conditions in section 1(2)(a) and (c)`

-- src:558 | (3) An employment officer shall, before making a relevant variation of a claimant commitment, notify the claimant of the proposed variation.
@ref s 44 JSA 10(3) (src:558)
GIVEN `the variation relates to information to be included in respect of the conditions in section 1(2)(a) and (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was notified of the proposed variation before it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 10(3) the employment officer has notified the claimant before making the variation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 44 JSA 10(4) the variation is a relevant variation` `the variation relates to information to be included in respect of the conditions in section 1(2)(a) and (c)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to notify "before making a relevant variation"; this variation is not one
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the claimant was notified of the proposed variation before it was made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, before making a relevant variation of a claimant commitment, notify the claimant of the proposed variation" -- a relevant variation made without prior notice
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:560 | (5) The employment officer may, and if asked to do so by the claimant in prescribed circumstances, shall forthwith refer a relevant variation of a claimant commitment proposed by the employment officer or requested by the claimant to the Secretary of State to determine—
-- src:561 | (a) whether, if the claimant were to act in accordance with the claimant commitment as proposed to be varied, he would satisfy—
-- src:562 | (i) the condition mentioned in section 1(2)(a), or
-- src:563 | (ii) the condition mentioned in section 1(2)(c), and
-- src:564 | (b) in the case of a variation proposed by the employment officer, whether it is reasonable to expect the claimant to have to act in accordance with the claimant commitment as proposed to be varied.
@ref s 44 JSA 10(5) (src:560-564)
GIVEN `the claimant has asked for the reference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant asked in prescribed circumstances` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 10(5) the employment officer must refer the proposed variation to the Secretary of State forthwith` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the claimant has asked for the reference`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, and if asked to do so by the claimant in prescribed circumstances, shall forthwith" -- no request, so a power and not a stated duty
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the claimant asked in prescribed circumstances`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): asked, but not in the prescribed circumstances, so the duty to refer does not arise
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the circumstances are prescribed in regulations that are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:566 | (a) shall, so far as practicable, dispose of it in accordance with this section before the end of the period of 14 days from the date of the reference,
@ref s 44 JSA 10(6)(a) (src:566)
GIVEN `the date of the reference` IS A DATE
      `the date the Secretary of State disposed of the reference` IS A DATE
      `it was practicable to dispose of it in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 10(6)(a) the Secretary of State has disposed of the reference in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the Secretary of State disposed of the reference` AT MOST `s 44 JSA 9(7)(a) the last day of the period of 14 days from the date of the reference` `the date of the reference`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, so far as practicable, dispose of it ... before the end of the period of 14 days" -- late when it was practicable to be in time
        IF `it was practicable to dispose of it in time`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so far as practicable"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:565 | (6) On a reference under subsection (5) the Secretary of State—
-- src:567 | (b) shall give such directions as he considers appropriate as to—
-- src:568 | (i) whether the claimant commitment should be varied, and
-- src:569 | (ii) if so, the terms on which the claimant is to accept the varied claimant commitment, and
@ref s 44 JSA 10(6)(b) (src:565 src:567-569)
GIVEN `a reference has been made under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 JSA 10(6)(b) the Secretary of State must give directions on whether and on what terms the claimant commitment is varied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a reference has been made under subsection (5)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On a reference under subsection (5)" -- no reference has been made
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:565 | (6) On a reference under subsection (5) the Secretary of State—
-- src:570 | (c) may direct that, if such conditions as he considers appropriate are satisfied, the claimant commitment, as proposed to be varied, is to be treated (if accepted) as having been accepted by the claimant on such date as may be specified in the direction.
@ref s 44 JSA 10(6)(c) (src:565 src:570)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has directed that the claimant commitment as proposed to be varied is to be treated as accepted on a date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions the direction sets are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant accepted it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified in the direction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 44 JSA 10(6)(c) the date on which the claimant commitment as varied is treated as accepted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the Secretary of State has directed that the claimant commitment as proposed to be varied is to be treated as accepted on a date`
           AND `the conditions the direction sets are satisfied`
           AND `the claimant accepted it`
        THEN JUST `the date specified in the direction`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if such conditions as he considers appropriate are satisfied ... (if accepted)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 44 JSA 10(3) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 44 JSA 10(3) notify the claimant of the proposed variation`

-- src:558 | (3) An employment officer shall, before making a relevant variation of a claimant commitment, notify the claimant of the proposed variation.
@ref s 44 JSA 10(3) (src:558)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `s 44 JSA 10(3) action`
`s 44 JSA 10(3) the employment officer must notify the claimant of a proposed relevant variation` MEANS
    PARTY `an employment officer`
    MUST `s 44 JSA 10(3) notify the claimant of the proposed variation`
    -- the text gives no number of days: the duty runs "before making a relevant variation", so no WITHIN is written (fork F-44-2)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `an employment officer` BECAUSE "a relevant variation was made without notifying the claimant of it beforehand"

§§ `s 44(5) JSA 35(1): employment officer`

-- src:576 | (5) In section 35 (interpretation), in subsection (1), after the definition of “employment” there is inserted—
-- src:577 | “employment officer”, for any purpose of this Act, means an officer of the Secretary of State or such other person as may be designated for that purpose by an order made by the Secretary of State;
@ref s 44(5) JSA 35(1) employment officer (src:576-577)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order made by the Secretary of State designates the person for that purpose` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44(5) JSA 35(1) the person is an employment officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an officer of the Secretary of State`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `an order made by the Secretary of State designates the person for that purpose`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employment officer” ... means an officer of the Secretary of State or such other person as may be designated" -- neither
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): designations are made by an order that is not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `s 45 Interviews`
-- s 45 substitutes words in JSA 8(1)(a) and (1A)(a): "attend at such place and at such time" becomes "participate in an interview in such manner, time and place".
-- JSA 8 is not among the sources; the substitution is an amendment of another Act (coverage row: inert, reason 2).
